Source diving yields to that unique occurrence of "enchantment failed" in  
the source (spell.c).

	case SPE_ENCHANT_WEAPON:
	case SPE_ENCHANT_ARMOR:
		if (role_skill >= P_EXPERT) n = 8;
		else if (role_skill >= P_SKILLED) n = 10;
		else if (role_skill >= P_BASIC) n = 12;
		else n = 14;	/* Unskilled or restricted */
		if (!rn2(n)) {
		    pseudo->blessed = 0;
		    (void) seffects(pseudo);
		} else
		    Your("enchantment failed!");
		break;

So, apparently, there is a random chance that the enchantment fails, the  
higher your skill, the smaller the chance.
rn2(n) reeturns a number 0 <= x < n, and the enchantment succeed only if  
this is 0.
So, if I've read the source properly (IIRSP ?), there is only 1 in 8  
chances of success at expert level.

